			"type": "text",
			"text": "Turritella is a turritellid sea snail which lived from the late Jurassic to the present day, with fossil and extant specied having been discovered across the world. Its name means “little-towered” in reference to its conical spiral shape, and in fact its family of Turritellidae is often known by the common name of “tower snails”. A prominent outcrop of this genus’s fossils is found at the Neogene Turritellenplatte in southwestern Germany."
